## Korea District Heating Corporation financial statements, 6 years: Back to a profit in 2023 after a net loss of KRW 184.0bn in 2022

The consolidated financial statements in the 2020–2025 annual reports that Korea District Heating Corporation (071320) filed with Korea's DART electronic disclosure system, laid out by year. Figures from the 2026 third-quarter report cover a different period and are shown separately. **Every figure below is taken as filed in the DART submissions; there is no interpretation or outlook.** Amounts are in Korean won (KRW; bn = billion, tn = trillion).

### 1. Income statement — the sign of net income changed in 2 years

| Fiscal year | Revenue | Revenue change | Operating income | Op. income change | Operating margin | Net income |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2020 | 2.10tn | — | 132.9bn | — | 6.3% | 27.9bn |
| 2021 | 2.54tn | +20.86% | 39.7bn | −70.13% | 1.6% | 21.5bn |
| 2022 | 4.17tn | +64.50% | −403.9bn | **turned to loss** | −9.7% | −184.0bn |
| 2023 | 3.95tn | −5.26% | 314.7bn | **turned to profit** | 8.0% | 199.4bn |
| 2024 | 3.57tn | −9.70% | 327.9bn | +4.20% | 9.2% | 209.9bn |
| 2025 | 4.00tn | +11.98% | 529.6bn | +61.50% | 13.2% | 338.9bn |

Revenue was largest in 2022 at KRW 4.17tn and smallest in 2020 at KRW 2.10tn among the six years. It fell from the previous year twice: 2023 (−5.26%), 2024 (−9.70%).

Operating income was largest in 2025 at KRW 529.6bn and smallest in 2022 at KRW −403.9bn. The operating margin was highest in 2025 at 13.2%.

**Net income was largest in 2025 at KRW 338.9bn and smallest in 2022 at KRW −184.0bn.**

### 2. Financial position — equity became 1.28x

| Fiscal year | Total assets | Total equity | Debt ratio | Current ratio |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2020 | 6.07tn | 1.80tn | 236.7% | 63.4% |
| 2021 | 6.52tn | 1.82tn | 257.5% | 47.0% |
| 2022 | 7.48tn | 1.67tn | 348.6% | 56.1% |
| 2023 | 7.97tn | 2.09tn | 280.7% | 44.4% |
| 2024 | 8.36tn | 2.27tn | 268.7% | 62.0% |
| 2025 | 8.23tn | 2.30tn | 257.6% | 51.1% |

The debt ratio was highest in 2022 at 348.6% and lowest in 2020 at 236.7%.

Over the same period total assets went from KRW 6.07tn to KRW 8.23tn (1.35x), and **total equity went from KRW 1.80tn to KRW 2.30tn and became 1.28x.**

The current ratio was below 100% in all six years — current liabilities exceeded current assets every year. It ranged from 44.4% to 63.4%.

